It is a basic router configuration with two interface
The router connects to two switches. Each switch connects two PCs. The router provides the default gateway for each LAN and forwards traffic between them
Devices:
1 x router
2 x switch 
4 x PCs
Networks:
LAN1 – 192.168.1.0 / 24
LAN2 – 192.168.2.0 / 24

Router Configuration:

enable
configure terminal

interface FastEthernet0/0
ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

interface FastEthernet0/1
ip address 192.168.2.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

PCs Configuration:
PC0 – 192.168.1.2   255.255.255.0
PC1 – 192.168.1.3   255.255.255.0
PC2 – 192.168.2.2   255.255.255.0
PC3 – 192.168.2.3   255.255.255.0

Testing :
Ping PC0 to PC1 to check communication between PCs in LAN 1
Ping PC2 to PC3 to check communication between PCs in LAN 2
Ping PC1 to PC3 to check communication between the two LANs through the router.




